{
  "tableVersion": 1,
  "recorded": "2026-11-15",
  "current_release": "v0.6.0",
  "note": "Cross-repo pin reference table for the toolkit, in the four classes of FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification#241. Each row records what this repository asserts: `sha256` and `bytes` are the digest and size of the pinned bytes, `local` is the vendored copy in this checkout, and `repository`, `revision` and `path` name the authoritative bytes to compare with - a tag for anything released, a commit for a draft contract or a suite. `bioheaders-pin-audit` reads this table and reports FRESH / DRIFT / ABSENT per row; it is data, not prose, reading it never writes it, and changing a value is a deliberate, dated commit. A row with no digest is a documented hole and reports ABSENT.",
  "out_of_scope": [
    "Dockerfile:17 pins the python:3.13-slim base image by digest, and release.yml and container.yml pin released toolkit bytes: container and package-version references, not contract bytes.",
    "plugins/ and galaxy/ version tokens follow the package version and are checked by tests/claude_plugin_test.py and .github/workflows/galaxy-tools.yml.",
    "fhr/ and the top-level compatibility copies mirror files inside this repository, so they are same-repo copies, not cross-repo references."
  ],
